class Solution {
    public String reverseWords(String s) {

        // Create a StringBuilder to store the final reversed sentence
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        // Start pointer from the end of the string
        int i = s.length() - 1;

        // Traverse the string from right to left
        while (i >= 0) {

            // Step 1: Skip all spaces
            // This handles trailing spaces and multiple spaces between words
            while (i >= 0 && s.charAt(i) == ' ') {
                i--;
            }

            // If pointer goes out of bounds, break (no more words)
            if (i < 0) break;

            // Step 2: Mark end of the current word
            int j = i;

            // Step 3: Move left until we find a space (start of word)
            while (i >= 0 && s.charAt(i) != ' ') {
                i--;
            }

            // Step 4: Add space before appending word (only if not first word)
            // This ensures no leading or trailing spaces
            if (result.length() > 0) {
                result.append(" ");
            }

            // Step 5: Extract and append the word
            // (i+1) is start of word, (j+1) is exclusive end
            result.append(s.substring(i + 1, j + 1));
        }

        // Convert StringBuilder to String and return
        return result.toString();
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(N), We traverse the string once from right to left and construct the result directly without extra passes.
Space Complexity: O(1),Ignoring the output string, no additional data structures proportional to input size are used.
